# Bridgehead greybox map (TASK-061, backlog B-025): rail bridge + depot at
# dusk (docs/07_VERTICAL_SLICE.md section 3). Terrain and force placement
# were built greybox-only by TASK-061; TASK-062 (backlog B-032) then added
# the real mission-sequence content once objective evaluation existed to
# consume it (see the `Objectives` note below). Terrain stays within the
# three fixed TerrainTileSet.Sources combinations (TASK-060): floor
# (passable, moveCost 1, opaque false), block (impassable, moveCost 0,
# opaque true), crate (passable, moveCost 3, opaque true).
#
# Layout: an impassable river runs north-south at x=8..9 for the whole map
# height, crossed by one compact two-cell-wide rail bridge deck at y=5..6
# (elevation 1) -- the single exposed approach. Friendly forces stage on
# the west bank (x<8); the depot (two building clusters plus scattered
# crate cover) occupies the east bank (x>=14), with an open lane in
# between that the machine-gun position overwatches.
#
# Friendly: agent 0 is the leader, agents 1-5 are five more soldiers --
# fireteam-alpha is agents 0/1/2, fireteam-bravo is agents 3/4/5 (TASK-059
# formation slots). Agent 4 conceptually carries the squad's support
# weapon (docs/07 "one support weapon suitable for suppression") and
# agent 5 the demolition charge ("one demolition interaction owned by the
# squad rather than a detailed inventory system") -- content labelling
# only in this comment; neither has a distinct simulation mechanic yet
# (task file "Inputs and assumptions").
#
# Enemy: agent 100 is the machine-gun team -- one agent representing the
# team, positioned to control the open lane immediately east of the
# bridge exit. Agents 101-104 are the four riflemen in prepared positions
# around the depot buildings.
#
# `Objectives` (TASK-062, backlog B-032) carries the real mission content
# TASK-061 deferred: the original placeholder optional `reach observation`
# entry (id 1, flavour/progress only -- observing the bridge area before
# committing, docs/07 section 3 step 1 -- never a success gate); a
# non-optional `destroy` against the `bridge-charge` target (id 2, 10-tick
# plant duration -- any Alive friendly agent occupying the target's own
# cell for 10 consecutive ticks satisfies it, `Simulation.mission`'s
# occupancy-based demolition, no new order type); a non-optional `extract`
# against the `extraction` area for every surviving friendly agent (id 3).
# Both id 2 and id 3 must be satisfied for `MissionOutcome` to reach
# `Succeeded`; `fail-on-friendly-eliminated true` (already authored) reaches
# `Failed` if every friendly agent goes down first.
